{"availability":"available","full":"sands-lab/nika","name":"nika","description":"A Network Arena for Benchmarking AI Agents on Network Troubleshooting","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":64,"forks":18,"created":"2025-12-18T12:31:36Z","updated":"2026-10-09T16:37:04Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://sands-lab.github.io/nika/","topics":[],"demo":"https://sands-lab.github.io/nika/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.987Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.987Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.987Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T16:43:31.987Z","stars":64,"forks":18}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["🤖 Overview · ✨ Features · 📦 Installation · 🚀 Quick start · 📖 Learn more · 🌐 Website · 📚 Cite","Think about SWE-Bench, but for network troubleshooting. NIKA, Network Incident Benchmark for AI Agents, is an open benchmark for agentic evals on network troubleshooting tasks. NIKA reproduces hundreds of realistic faults covering data center networks, campus networks, ISP backbones, SDN fabrics, overlay networks, and Kubernetes CNIs. It connects any agent directly to a live network stack while the incident is ongoing, evaluating the ability of the AI agent to troubleshoot the network using network diagnostic tools, switch CLIs, and network telemetry data. You don't need physical hardware to…","NIKA lets you plug in any LLM or agent framework and measure its operational capability under identical, reproducible conditions."],"features":["💬 Network Manager \"A vendor is pitching me an AI solution for network operations. It passes all the standard telecom benchmarks (TeleQnA, TeleLogs, TeleMath, 3GPP-TSG), but I need objective evidence it can handle real…","💬 Network SRE \"I respond to network incidents every day. I want an AI agent to help, but I'm not sure it will understand my topology or make things worse.\"","💬 AI Researcher \"I'm designing a new harness for long-horizon network tasks. I need a benchmark to ablate components, measure reproducibly, and compare against published baselines.\"","💬 Applied ML Engineer \"I want to fine-tune an open-source model on network troubleshooting and need a structured dataset paired with a rigorous evaluation framework.\"","💬 Contributor \"I want to contribute a new network scenario or fault type to the community and have it evaluated systematically.\""],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sands-lab/nika/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"71a74876ef64a748006f521fb0569c7dff0aa475bac7422e9803ddaec9eea57e","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:32.062Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:32.062Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"🤖 Overview · ✨ Features · 📦 Installation · 🚀 Quick start · 📖 Learn more · 🌐 Website · 📚 Cite","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sands-lab/nika/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"71a74876ef64a748006f521fb0569c7dff0aa475bac7422e9803ddaec9eea57e","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sands-lab/nika/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:32.063Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T16:37:04Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/sands-lab/nika/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T16:43:32.064Z","hash":"71a74876ef64a748006f521fb0569c7dff0aa475bac7422e9803ddaec9eea57e","originalBytes":15005,"storedBytes":15005,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["network","nika","agent","docs","run","benchmark","operations","agents","failure","config","env","fault","scenario","see","telemetry","any","benchmarks","containerlab","extra","key","live","shell","troubleshooting","api","basic","custom","incident","offline","reference","remote","want","incidents","injection","install","new","nika.yaml","online","their","tools","types","variants","yaml","agentic","cli","emulation","evals","kathar","lab","leaderboard","llm","mcp","need","openai","operational","provider","sandboxing","settings","sta